# Extra apt packages for the R Station print server (see ../../PRINT_SERVER.md).
# Appended to the platform's package list at build time. Hotfix bundles can't
# install packages, so adding or changing anything here means a full image.

# The print system. The print server talks to it over IPP on localhost:631
# (backend/cups_client.py) — no other client library is needed.
cups

# The PDF -> printer filters CUPS uses to print the PDFs the website renders.
cups-filters

# Printer drivers, so Settings > Printers' "Find a specific driver" search has something to
# offer printers that aren't driverless (backend/printer_setup.py, `drivers`). A curated
# set rather than printer-driver-all, which drags in the whole HPLIP stack: foomatic's PPD
# database (the Brother/Ricoh/Kyocera/etc. PCL6 and PostScript entries — the biggest single
# win), plus the open-source drivers that cover most of what donors actually hand over.
# Printers that speak IPP Everywhere / AirPrint still need none of this.
foomatic-db-compressed-ppds
printer-driver-gutenprint
printer-driver-brlaser
printer-driver-pxljr
printer-driver-foo2zjs
printer-driver-splix
printer-driver-escpr
printer-driver-c2esp
printer-driver-postscript-hp
printer-driver-hpcups
# Label printers (Dymo, Brother P-touch) — the website prints labels too.
printer-driver-dymo
printer-driver-ptouch

# Colour emoji. The website uses emoji as icons; without a font, Chromium draws blank boxes.
fonts-noto-color-emoji

# The offline local server (Settings > Local server; ../../LOCAL_SERVER.md): the container engine and
# Compose to run the stack baked in by build-offline-bundle.sh, and curl for the supervisor's health
# probe. Their units are overridden (system/docker.service,
# docker.socket) so none of it runs unless that page has been switched on.
docker.io
docker-compose
curl
